    <h2>What We Do</h2>
    <p>BikeLabs covers four things: gear reviews, motorcycle guides, workshop how-tos, and moto culture. Every piece of content is written to answer a real question a rider might have — not to fill a content calendar.</p>
    <p>We test gear across different riding conditions, compare motorcycles side by side, publish step-by-step maintenance guides, and cover the routes and culture that make riding worth doing in the first place. We also build <a href="{{ '/tools/' | url }}">free calculators</a> — gearing, tyre sizing, fuel range, fitment — so you can run the numbers on your own bike before spending money.</p>

    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>A small team of riders with an outsized obsession with motorcycles. We ride everything from budget Asian commuters to premium adventure bikes. We source gear globally — including from Asia, where the best value in motorcycle equipment often sits.</p>
    <p>We're based in Southeast Asia, which gives us a different lens on riding than most Western moto media. The bikes are different here. The conditions are different. The prices are different. We write for a global audience but we don't pretend the world looks the same from every saddle.</p>

    <h2>Our Standards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Honest verdicts.</strong> If something isn't worth buying, we say so.</li>
      <li><strong>Transparency.</strong> When we test a product, we tell you how and under what conditions — see <a href="{{ '/how-we-test/' | url }}">How We Test</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Independence.</strong> We do not accept payment for coverage or verdicts. Affiliate commissions never influence a review's conclusion.</li>
      <li><strong>Long-form over clickbait.</strong> Our reviews aim to be the last thing you need to read before making a decision.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How We Make Money</h2>
    <p>BikeLabs is funded by advertising and affiliate commissions. When you buy a product through one of our links, we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. We disclose this on every article that contains affiliate links, and it has no bearing on what we recommend — several of our top picks earn us nothing at all.</p>

    <h2>Work With Us</h2>
    <p>We're open to working with brands on honest, rider-focused content. If you have a product you'd like reviewed or want to collaborate on a feature, reach out — we give every product a fair test and an honest write-up. What we don't offer: paid verdicts, guaranteed positive coverage, or undisclosed sponsorships.</p>
    <p>Get in touch at <a href="mailto:info@bikelabs.com"><strong>info@bikelabs.com</strong></a>.</p>

    <h2>Get In Touch</h2>
    <p>Got a tip, a correction, or a bike you think we should test? Reach us at <a href="mailto:info@bikelabs.com"><strong>info@bikelabs.com</strong></a>. We read everything, and we publish corrections when we get something wrong.</p>

